00:56:30.620 --> 00:56:37.740
So in The Convict, there is a deleted talking head where Creed says that he's been to prison.
在《The Convict》那一集里，有一个被删掉的采访片段，克里德说他坐过牢。

1137
00:56:37.920 --> 00:56:39.820
And in fact, that's where he got his name.
事实上，他的名字就是在那儿得来的。

1138
00:56:40.080 --> 00:56:41.280
Creed was in prison.
克里德坐过牢。

1139
00:56:42.960 --> 00:56:46.260
Meaning that, like, Creed is not his given name.
也就是说，克里德并不是他的本名。

1140
00:56:46.260 --> 00:56:48.440
It's just the name he got in prison.
那只是他在监狱里得到的代号。

1141
00:56:48.640 --> 00:56:49.660
He doesn't go into it.
他没有细说。

1142
00:56:49.760 --> 00:56:50.560
We don't know why.
我们不知道原因。

1143
00:56:50.820 --> 00:56:58.660
And then he goes on to say that he used to make a type of wine called Pruno in the toilets.
接着他说他以前在马桶里酿过一种叫“普鲁诺”的酒。

1144
00:56:59.060 --> 00:57:01.780
And it's made of fruit, sugar, and ketchup.
是用水果、糖和番茄酱做的。

1145
00:57:02.200 --> 00:57:04.440
And he really misses that wine.
他真的很怀念那种酒。

1146
00:57:04.880 --> 00:57:05.560
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1147
00:57:07.540 --> 00:57:08.060
Pruno.
普鲁诺酒。

1148
00:57:08.060 --> 00:57:11.820
That actually made my stomach turn when you said ketchup.
你提到番茄酱的时候，我胃里真是一阵翻江倒海。

1149
00:57:12.080 --> 00:57:13.060
It's so disgusting.
太恶心了。

1150
00:57:13.420 --> 00:57:14.780
I mean, it started with toilet.
我是说，光是“马桶”这两个字就已经够恶心了。

1151
00:57:15.320 --> 00:57:18.760
And then it went full circle when you said ketchup.
然后当你提到番茄酱时，一切又回到了原点。

1152
00:57:19.500 --> 00:57:20.340
Creed making Pruno.
克里德在酿造普鲁诺酒。

1153
00:57:20.780 --> 00:57:33.260
Well, this is interesting because that would be at odds with the booze crew's deleted talking head in which Creed admits to being himself, Creed Bratton, from the grassroots.
嗯，这很有趣，因为这与“酒鬼小分队”那段被删减的采访片段相矛盾，在那段里克里德承认他就是他自己，那个来自草根阶层的克里德·布拉顿。

1154
00:57:33.260 --> 00:57:37.420
But both of those talking heads were deleted, so I guess it doesn't matter.
但那两段采访都被删了，所以我想这无所谓了。

1155
00:57:37.860 --> 00:57:39.340
I think with Creed, nothing matters.
我觉得对于克里德来说，什么都无所谓。

1156
00:57:39.540 --> 00:57:40.260
All bets are off.
一切皆有可能。

1157
00:57:40.380 --> 00:57:41.420
He lives under a desk.
他住在办公桌底下。

1158
00:57:41.600 --> 00:57:42.500
He lives in Toronto.
他住在多伦多。

1159
00:57:42.500 --> 00:57:43.920
We don't know where he lives.
我们根本不知道他住哪儿。

1160
00:57:44.600 --> 00:57:47.020
He's got multiple names, identities.
他有好几个名字和身份。

1161
00:57:47.560 --> 00:57:49.120
And you know what's great about Creed?
你知道克里德最棒的一点是什么吗？

1162
00:57:49.340 --> 00:57:52.380
I think from the writer's standpoint is that it didn't matter.
我想从编剧的角度来看，就是这些都无所谓。

1163
00:57:53.000 --> 00:57:53.440
Yes.
没错。

1164
00:57:53.660 --> 00:57:55.980
Because you never know if Creed's telling the truth or not.
因为你永远不知道克里德说的是不是真话。

1165
00:57:56.420 --> 00:57:58.220
It's such a fun character to write for.
为这个角色写剧本真的很有趣。

1166
00:57:58.440 --> 00:57:58.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1167
00:57:58.720 --> 00:58:02.400
So the other deleted scene, which is so good, Jenna.
所以另一个被删减的片段，真的非常棒，珍娜。

1168
00:58:02.660 --> 00:58:06.220
You know, Jenna, you keep saying you have a new appreciation for the character of Ryan.
你知道吗，珍娜，你一直说你对瑞安这个角色有了新的认识。

1169
00:58:06.700 --> 00:58:07.120
Yes.
是的。

1170
00:58:07.540 --> 00:58:08.940
Well, for me, it's Phyllis.
对我来说，那个人是菲利斯。

1171
00:58:09.440 --> 00:58:09.880
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1172
00:58:09.960 --> 00:58:11.040
I can't get enough of her.
我真是怎么看她都看不够。

1173
00:58:11.300 --> 00:58:15.180
So there is this deleted moment between Pam and Phyllis and the convict.
所以有一个帕姆、菲利斯和那个罪犯之间被删减的片段。

1174
00:58:15.520 --> 00:58:17.780
Michael has locked everyone in the conference room.
迈克尔把所有人都锁在了会议室里。

1175
00:58:18.140 --> 00:58:22.680
And in the deleted scenes, there's a real passage of time that doesn't happen in the episode.
在这些删减片段中，有一段真实的时间流逝，但在正片里并没有表现出来。

1176
00:58:22.860 --> 00:58:27.940
I guess we just didn't have enough time, you know, in the 21 minutes and 30 seconds that we get.
我想我们只是没有足够的时间，你知道，在我们要完成的21分30秒的时长里。

1177
00:58:27.940 --> 00:58:29.580
But like what Dave was saying.
但就像戴夫刚才说的那样。

1178
00:58:29.860 --> 00:58:30.040
Yeah.
是啊。

1179
00:58:30.200 --> 00:58:31.760
So they have to really truncate it.
所以他们必须得大幅删减。

1180
00:58:31.880 --> 00:58:37.020
But there's this great scene where Phyllis is showing Pam her engagement ring.
但有一个很棒的场景，菲利斯在向帕姆展示她的订婚戒指。

1181
00:58:37.260 --> 00:58:39.160
And Jenna, it's not a cluster.
而且珍娜，那不是碎钻拼成的。

1182
00:58:39.480 --> 00:58:40.520
It's not a cluster?
不是碎钻拼的？

1183
00:58:40.980 --> 00:58:41.880
We knew it.
我们早就知道了。

1184
00:58:42.000 --> 00:58:42.600
We called it.
我们猜到了。

1185
00:58:42.740 --> 00:58:43.500
It's not a cluster.
那不是碎钻拼的。

1186
00:58:43.820 --> 00:58:48.720
It is an enormous marquee engagement ring.
那是一枚巨大的马眼形订婚戒指。

1187
00:58:49.000 --> 00:58:50.040
Huge marquee diamond.
巨大的马眼形钻石。

1188
00:58:50.400 --> 00:58:52.380
And in fact, she brags to Pam.
事实上，她还向帕姆炫耀。

1189
00:58:52.560 --> 00:58:55.620
She's like, you know, this is the most expensive type of diamond.
她说，你知道吗，这是最昂贵的那种钻石。

1190
00:58:55.620 --> 00:58:58.700
And Bob wanted to get me even a bigger one.
鲍勃本来还想给我买个更大的。

1191
00:58:59.100 --> 00:59:01.920
This makes so much more sense.
这下一切都说得通了。

1192
00:59:02.080 --> 00:59:09.260
In that very first scene, when she tells Michael that she's engaged, she had that little cluster on her finger.
在最开始的那场戏里，当她告诉迈克尔她订婚时，她手指上戴的是那种小碎钻拼成的戒指。

1193
00:59:09.460 --> 00:59:10.900
They did not have her ring yet.
他们当时还没拿到她的那枚戒指。

1194
00:59:11.100 --> 00:59:12.060
That is, that is.
就是这样，就是这样。

1195
00:59:12.220 --> 00:59:12.420
Clearly.
很明显。

1196
00:59:12.720 --> 00:59:17.140
And it makes sense that she would have a big old diamond from Bob Vance of Vance Refrigeration.
而且她戴着鲍勃·万斯（万斯制冷公司的鲍勃）送的一枚大钻戒才合理嘛。

1197
00:59:17.720 --> 00:59:18.200
Yes.
没错。

1198
00:59:18.720 --> 00:59:19.200
Oh.
哦。

1199
00:59:20.180 --> 00:59:21.820
Oh, I wish they'd kept that in.
哦，真希望他们能把那段留着。

1200
00:59:22.180 --> 00:59:22.280
Yeah.
是啊。

1201
00:59:22.360 --> 00:59:23.160
And it's really fun.
而且真的很有趣。

1202
00:59:23.300 --> 00:59:23.860
It's really cute.
真的很可爱。

1203
00:59:23.960 --> 00:59:25.960
She's so, so proud of it.
她对此感到非常、非常自豪。

1204
00:59:27.180 --> 00:59:27.780
All right.
好吧。

1205
00:59:27.880 --> 00:59:31.400
Well, Angela, now people have a gripe with us.
那么，安吉拉，现在人们对我们有意见了。

1206
00:59:31.520 --> 00:59:32.360
What do we do?
我们该怎么办？

1207
00:59:32.640 --> 00:59:35.960
It's about our assessment of wishy-washy Jim.
是关于我们对优柔寡断的吉姆的评价。

1208
00:59:36.220 --> 00:59:38.020
Oh, well, I thought that might be coming.
哦，好吧，我想到可能会有这种情况。

1209
00:59:38.320 --> 00:59:40.260
Crystal Nichols wrote in to say,
克里斯托·尼科尔斯写信来说，

1210
00:59:40.260 --> 00:59:45.840
I don't think Jim is wishy-washy, nor does he owe Pam an explanation about Karen.
我不觉得吉姆优柔寡断，他也不欠帕姆一个关于凯伦的解释。

1211
00:59:46.240 --> 00:59:47.320
Amy Durham agrees.
艾米·达勒姆表示赞同。

1212
00:59:47.560 --> 00:59:54.040
Pam flirted with Jim and established intimacy with him for seasons one through three, but then always went home to Roy.
帕姆在第一到第三季里一直和吉姆调情并保持亲密关系，但最后总是回到罗伊身边。

1213
00:59:54.320 --> 00:59:56.700
Oh, well, that's, there's some truth there.
哦，好吧，这，这确实有一定道理。

1214
00:59:57.060 --> 01:00:05.300
Bronte thinks that there are times when Jim is downright mean or disrespectful and doesn't think that he should always be called a nice guy.
布朗特认为，有时吉姆确实表现得刻薄或不尊重人，不认为他总该被称为好人。

1215
01:00:05.300 --> 01:00:13.280
But Emily Hubbard defends Jim by saying he is making an effort to be friends with Pam while not crossing the line into flirtation.
但艾米丽·哈伯德为吉姆辩护说，他是在努力和帕姆做朋友，同时没有越界去调情。

1216
01:00:13.640 --> 01:00:18.480
He likewise doesn't lay it on thick with Karen in front of Pam out of respect.
出于尊重，他同样没有在帕姆面前和凯伦表现得过于亲昵。

1217
01:00:18.800 --> 01:00:24.800
But since Pam kept Jim on the hook for so long, he's right not to do the same thing to Pam in return.
但既然帕姆让吉姆苦等了那么久，他没必要反过来对帕姆做同样的事，他是对的。

1218
01:00:25.040 --> 01:00:28.800
I think it's just people are pointing out Pam started the wishy-washy.
我觉得大家只是在指出，是帕姆先开始优柔寡断的。

1219
01:00:28.800 --> 01:00:38.400
Pam, her wishy-washiness to me was like another level because she was engaged in living with someone.
帕姆，她对我的那种优柔寡断是另一个层面的，因为她当时已经订婚并和别人住在一起了。

1220
01:00:40.040 --> 01:00:47.160
And I know her heart was like falling for Jim and she was having sort of almost like this emotional affair.
我知道她的心已经倾向于吉姆了，她当时几乎是在进行一场精神出轨。

1221
01:00:48.060 --> 01:00:50.760
But she was 100% having an emotional affair.
但她百分之百是在精神出轨。

1222
01:00:50.900 --> 01:00:52.400
Yeah, exactly.
是的，没错。

1223
01:00:52.400 --> 01:00:57.860
And then also trying to figure out like, well, I've put so much time in with Roy.
而且她当时也在纠结，比如，好吧，我在罗伊身上投入了这么多时间。

1224
01:00:57.860 --> 01:01:00.280
So she was definitely doing all this waffling.
所以她绝对是在反复摇摆。

1225
01:01:00.700 --> 01:01:03.760
And then, I don't know, it's really hard.
而且，我不知道，这真的很难。

1226
01:01:03.980 --> 01:01:06.020
This is the star-crossed lover story.
这就是一段苦命鸳鸯的故事。

1227
01:01:06.340 --> 01:01:08.180
Well, we have a final thought.
好吧，我们有一个最后的想法。

1228
01:01:08.300 --> 01:01:08.580
Okay.
好的。

1229
01:01:08.960 --> 01:01:11.400
From Randall Robertson, who wrote this.
来自兰德尔·罗伯逊，他写道：

1230
01:01:12.140 --> 01:01:15.340
I'm coming to the defense of Jim being wishy-washy.
我来为吉姆的优柔寡断辩护。

1231
01:01:16.020 --> 01:01:18.420
Don't you ladies remember young love?
女士们，你们不记得年轻时的爱情了吗？

1232
01:01:19.120 --> 01:01:20.800
Pam was Jim's everything.
帕姆是吉姆的一切。

1233
01:01:20.800 --> 01:01:24.660
He told her he loved her and then kissed her and she kissed him back.
他告诉她他爱她，然后吻了她，她也回吻了他。

1234
01:01:24.660 --> 01:01:27.620
She then told him she was going to still marry Roy.
然后她告诉他，她还是要嫁给罗伊。

1235
01:01:28.160 --> 01:01:34.420
Pam tore Jim's heart into a million pieces, then put those pieces in a shredder behind her desk.
帕姆把吉姆的心撕成了碎片，然后把这些碎片放进了她办公桌后的碎纸机里。

1236
01:01:35.040 --> 01:01:36.320
Karen is a rebound.
凯伦只是个过渡。

1237
01:01:36.560 --> 01:01:42.320
And now he has to be in the same space as the woman who put him in his heartbroken state.
现在他必须和那个让他心碎的女人待在同一个空间里。

1238
01:01:42.880 --> 01:01:48.160
When you have no heart to give anyone, all you get is wishy-washy.
当你没有心可以给任何人时，你剩下的就只有优柔寡断了。

1239
01:01:49.460 --> 01:01:50.660
Randall Robertson.
兰德尔·罗伯逊。

1240
01:01:50.660 --> 01:01:52.860
And that was amazing.
那太棒了。

1241
01:01:53.120 --> 01:01:53.920
And it's true.
而且那是真的。

1242
01:01:54.120 --> 01:01:55.320
We were too hard on Jim.
我们对吉姆太苛刻了。

1243
01:01:55.560 --> 01:01:57.100
Randall, that last line.
兰德尔，最后那句话。

1244
01:01:57.380 --> 01:02:00.980
When you have no heart to give anyone, all you get is wishy-washy.
当你没有心可以给任何人时，你剩下的就只有优柔寡断了。

1245
01:02:01.460 --> 01:02:01.740
Yeah.
是的。

1246
01:02:02.160 --> 01:02:07.240
Well, there was a little bit of debate, Jenna, about whether or not Toby outed Oscar
好吧，珍娜，关于托比是否曝光了奥斯卡，或者他在《同性恋猎巫》那一集中是否得到了奥斯卡的许可才透露他是同性恋，我们有一点争论。

1247
01:02:07.240 --> 01:02:12.880
or if he had Oscar's permission to disclose he was gay in the gay witch hunt episode.
或者他在《同性恋猎巫》那一集中是否得到了奥斯卡的许可才透露他是同性恋。

1248
01:02:13.020 --> 01:02:15.900
We were giving Toby a lot of grief about this, remember?
我们当时因为这件事给了托比很多压力，还记得吗？

1249
01:02:15.900 --> 01:02:16.480
Yes.
记得。

1250
01:02:16.720 --> 01:02:23.980
Emily Zaloom says, 100% Oscar outed Oscar, to which Caitlin Workman and Annie Day both point out,
艾米丽·扎卢姆说，百分之百是奥斯卡自己曝光的，对此凯特琳·沃克曼和安妮·戴都指出，

1251
01:02:24.180 --> 01:02:27.580
at the end of Toby and Michael's conversation, Toby says,
在托比和迈克尔谈话结束时，托比说，

1252
01:02:27.940 --> 01:02:30.760
Oscar obviously hopes he can count on your discretion,
奥斯卡显然希望你能守口如瓶，

1253
01:02:31.320 --> 01:02:36.240
which they think sort of implies that Oscar gave Toby permission to tell Michael.
他们认为这暗示了奥斯卡允许托比告诉迈克尔。

1254
01:02:36.240 --> 01:02:41.260
So Toby saying, Oscar hopes he can count on you.
所以托比说，奥斯卡希望你能守口如瓶。

1255
01:02:41.380 --> 01:02:42.420
To be discreet.
要谨慎行事。

1256
01:02:42.620 --> 01:02:47.240
Means, I guess, that maybe, filling in the blanks, Toby said to Oscar,
我想这意味着，填补空白的话，托比可能对奥斯卡说，

1257
01:02:47.500 --> 01:02:50.940
do you mind if I share this information with Michael?
你不介意我把这个消息告诉迈克尔吧？

1258
01:02:50.940 --> 01:02:54.760
To which Oscar said, yes, but please ask him.
奥斯卡回答说，可以，但请你问问他。

1259
01:02:54.820 --> 01:02:56.340
I would appreciate his discretion.
我会很感激他的谨慎。

1260
01:02:56.620 --> 01:02:57.480
I don't buy it.
我不信。

1261
01:02:57.580 --> 01:03:01.160
I don't think Oscar would trust Michael with anything about his personal life.
我不认为奥斯卡会把任何私生活的事告诉迈克尔。

1262
01:03:01.160 --> 01:03:01.920
You know what?
你知道吗？

1263
01:03:02.140 --> 01:03:09.240
Even more, I think Toby has to be like, okay, let's say I do have Oscar's permission.
更进一步说，我觉得托比当时肯定在想，好吧，假设我确实得到了奥斯卡的许可。

1264
01:03:09.900 --> 01:03:13.960
Is this still the conversation I should have with Michael?
这还是我应该和迈克尔进行的谈话吗？

1265
01:03:14.100 --> 01:03:16.780
I mean, he kind of has to have the conversation, right?
我的意思是，他必须得进行这次谈话，对吧？

1266
01:03:16.940 --> 01:03:19.200
Because he has to speak to Michael about his behavior.
因为他必须就迈克尔的行为和他谈谈。

1267
01:03:20.320 --> 01:03:23.480
Well, gosh, now I think they're right.
天哪，现在我觉得他们是对的。

1268
01:03:24.280 --> 01:03:29.720
Like the more you're talking, now I'm like, oh, oh, yeah, Toby had to say something.
你越说，我现在就越觉得，哦，哦，没错，托比确实得说点什么。

1269
01:03:30.020 --> 01:03:32.340
And Oscar was like, okay, well, if you tell him, it's okay.
而奥斯卡当时的态度是，好吧，如果你要告诉他，那没问题。

1270
01:03:32.720 --> 01:03:32.940
Okay.
好吧。

1271
01:03:33.040 --> 01:03:34.100
Guys, I see it.
伙计们，我明白了。

1272
01:03:34.180 --> 01:03:34.680
I see it.
我明白了。

1273
01:03:34.800 --> 01:03:39.140
Well, listen, I wanted to throw out a couple of tidbits that people sent in that I found really
听着，我想分享几个听众发来的小趣事，我觉得非常

1274
01:03:39.140 --> 01:03:39.960
fun and interesting.
有趣且引人入胜。

1275
01:03:40.120 --> 01:03:42.880
